= Introduction

The spectral lines of a given source is in some sort like a fingerprint. With the information of the spectral lines one can with a high certainty determine with which source we are dealing with. In this little experiment we are doing a similar thing .  We want to analyze the sun spectre which is well known and want to search some "dips" in the spectre. This are the absorption lines which are caused due to the atmosphere of the sun and earth. This gives us a better understanding on the use cases of the absorption lines. 


Using the same ideas we want to analyze a simple unknown source by analyzing the emerging spectral lines. We will do this in the simplest case possible, where there is only one element. This allows us to focus on the fundamental principle without getting it to complicated.  With multiples elements this approach can get  very tidies and complicated.In such cases one required more advanced method of analyzing, which is nor our focus in this experiment.

